<title>JAPAN: Japan May M2+CD money supply up 3.0 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan May M2+CD money supply up 3.0 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.0 percent in May from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of May money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     MAY PRELIM   APR REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.0	   +3.2</p>
<p>   M1			 +9.0	   +8.8</p>
<p>   CDs		     +29.5	  +23.8</p>
<p>Broadest Liquidity	+3.6	   +4.0</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     MAY PRELIM   APR REVISED</p>
<p>Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +2.7	   +8.0</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			     MAY PRELIM   APR REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs	568.9 trln   570.0 trln</p>
<p>   M1			178.9 trln   178.6 trln</p>
<p>   CDs			20.8 trln    24.4 trln</p>
<p>			     MAY PRELIM   APR REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity     1,151.2 trln 1,152.0 trln</p>
<p>(NOTE: The broadest liquidity measure includes postal savings deposits at agricultural financial institutions and trust banks, bank debentures, Japanese government bonds, investment trusts and foreign bonds, along with M2 plus CDs.)</p>
</text>
